# Line endings are the repository's, not the checkout's.
#
# Git's `core.autocrlf` gave this repository CRLF working trees on Windows,
# and three separate guards then failed on a clean checkout: two matched
# `\n` against `\r\n` and read nothing, and esbuild refused to parse a CRLF
# `.mjs` at all ("Invalid or unexpected token", pointing at a comment) — so
# `tests/tools/mutate-guard.test.ts` collected zero tests. Nineteen failures
# about the platform, none about the product, on a suite whose whole job is
# telling those apart. See backlog `the-suite-assumes-a-posix-checkout`.
#
# The blob content is already LF; this only stops it being converted on the
# way out, so no committed file changes.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, and must never be line-ending converted.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
